    "tranche": "T3",
    "tranche_reason": "Compares an adaptive optimizer with SGD on Indonesian inflation forecasting, extending the optimizer comparison to a time-series forecasting setting.",
    "gate_note": "The study compares SGD and AdaGrad using training and testing forecast errors. It does not test random-label memorization, network width, convolutional versus fully connected architectures, batch size, dropout, sharpness, or removal of memorized examples.",
    "test_reason": "The study directly compares SGD and adaptive AdaGrad on training and held-out prediction errors, extending V4's optimizer comparison to inflation forecasting.",
    "authors_conclusion": "The record accurately paraphrases the optimizer conclusion: the authors say SGD gives more accurate and stable predictions than AdaGrad, with lower training and testing errors. Stability is their interpretation; no separate stability measure is reported.",
    "recipe": "different",
    "recipe_differences": "The study compares SGD with AdaGrad rather than the cited Adam-to-SGD switch; task is inflation time-series forecasting, with one learning rate and epoch setting reported for the comparison.",
    "method_sensitivity": "Optimizer comparison is reported at learning rate 0.05, 200 epochs, and logistic activation; no alternative settings for this comparison are reported.",
